fix: add notsecret comments to NetBox env files

Add '# notsecret' comments to all password and secret lines in NetBox
environment files to prevent GitHub secret scanning alerts.

These are demo/workshop credentials, not production secrets. The notsecret
comment tells security scanners (gitleaks/PwnedAlert) to ignore these lines.

Files updated:
- netbox-docker/env/redis.env
- netbox-docker/env/redis-cache.env
- netbox-docker/env/postgres.env
- netbox-docker/env/netbox.env (DB_PASSWORD, REDIS_PASSWORD, REDIS_CACHE_PASSWORD, SECRET_KEY, API_TOKEN_PEPPERS)

Per Red Hat InfoSec pattern distribution server documentation:
https://source.redhat.com/departments/it/it-information-security/wiki/pattern_distribution_server
